  "content": {
    "id": "p50-q9-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Find the divisors of $10x^2 + 3x - 25$ that leave a remainder of 2.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x-\\frac{3}{2}$ or $x+\\frac{9}{5}$. Use $P(c)=2$ to obtain $(2c-3)(5c+9)=0$.",
      "worked": "For a divisor $x-c$, the remainder theorem gives $P(c)=2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}10c^2+3c-25&=2\\\\10c^2+3c-27&=0\\\\(2c-3)(5c+9)&=0\\\\c&=\\frac{3}{2}\\text{ or }-\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe divisors are $x-\\frac{3}{2}$ or $x+\\frac{9}{5}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
